From: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: preserve resources across color-only updates

Disabling the built-in display on Gaokun3 can update the remaining DP
CRTC's color state without a modeset. Releasing and reserving resources
then moves its CTL while the physical encoder retains the old CTL.
Captured traces show CRTC 91 assigned CTL_0 while encoder 37 flushes
CTL_1 with an empty pending mask, followed by IOMMU faults and underruns.

Keep the existing resources for color-only updates. Request a modeset
when CTM/gamma changes alter the need for DSPPs so the encoder receives
the new resource assignment. Clear mixer DSPP pointers when the new
allocation no longer includes them.

The same root cause and allocation rule are described in the upstream
proposal linked below, found after this fix was tested on Gaokun3.
This local change also clears released DSPP pointers and retains the
existing msm_atomic_check() behavior.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260912-fd-kms-fix-smmu-v3-7-a7ddc6fe2032@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1480,8 +1480,8 @@
 
 		cstate->mixers[i].hw_lm = to_dpu_hw_mixer(hw_lm[i]);
 		cstate->mixers[i].lm_ctl = to_dpu_hw_ctl(hw_ctl[ctl_idx]);
-		if (i < num_dspp)
-			cstate->mixers[i].hw_dspp = to_dpu_hw_dspp(hw_dspp[i]);
+		cstate->mixers[i].hw_dspp = i < num_dspp ?
+			to_dpu_hw_dspp(hw_dspp[i]) : NULL;
 	}
 
 	cstate->num_mixers = num_lm;
@@ -1503,6 +1503,8 @@
 	struct drm_crtc *crtc = new_crtc_state->crtc;
 	bool clone_mode_enabled = drm_crtc_in_clone_mode(old_crtc_state);
 	bool clone_mode_requested = drm_crtc_in_clone_mode(new_crtc_state);
+	bool old_dspp = old_crtc_state->ctm || old_crtc_state->gamma_lut;
+	bool new_dspp = new_crtc_state->ctm || new_crtc_state->gamma_lut;
 
 	DRM_DEBUG_ATOMIC("%d\n", crtc->base.id);
 
@@ -1512,6 +1514,10 @@
 			new_crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
 	}
 
+	/* A change in DSPP requirements needs new resources and encoder setup. */
+	if (old_dspp != new_dspp)
+		new_crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
+
 	if ((clone_mode_requested && !clone_mode_enabled) ||
 	    (!clone_mode_requested && clone_mode_enabled))
 		new_crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
@@ -1534,9 +1540,8 @@
 
 	bool needs_dirtyfb = dpu_crtc_needs_dirtyfb(crtc_state);
 
-	/* don't reallocate resources if only ACTIVE has beeen changed */
-	if (crtc_state->mode_changed || crtc_state->connectors_changed ||
-	    crtc_state->color_mgmt_changed) {
+	/* Color updates keep the resources installed by the last modeset. */
+	if (crtc_state->mode_changed || crtc_state->connectors_changed) {
 		rc = dpu_crtc_assign_resources(crtc, crtc_state);
 		if (rc < 0)
 			return rc;
